# Settings, Files (docs/SETUP.md "Where OpenSE4 keeps its own files"): the folder in use and the
# rule that chose it (a script run's own folder, from OPENSE4_USER_DIR, which comes before a
# portable copy: the switch is dim); a saves folder of the player's, a folder that cannot be
# made refused, and Default. The portable switch itself plays in portable-copy.script.
# ci: fixture-data (it needs nothing but our own content: CI plays it on the test fixtures)
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --layout=1024x768 --size=1024x768

wait-screen front
click item:Settings in=front
click item:Files in=front
wait-for item:user-folder:OPENSE4_USER_DIR
assert-disabled item:"Keep saves and settings in OpenSE4's folder"
# A saves folder inside the user folder.
click item:##savesfolder
type "My Saves"
click item:Use
wait-for item:"Saved games now go to *My Saves."
# A folder under a file cannot be made: refused, the folder in use stays.
click item:##savesfolder
key Ctrl+A
type "settings.toml/Saves"
click item:Use
wait-for item:"*settings.toml*Saves cannot be made*"
click item:Default
wait-for item:"Saved games go to *saves again."
click item:Back in=front
wait-for item:Settings in=front
